                "senderName": "NWS Missoula MT",
                "headline": "Flood Watch issued September 8 at 7:36AM MDT until September 8 at 12:00PM MDT by NWS Missoula MT",
                "description": "* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...A portion of northwest Montana, including the following\narea, West Glacier Region including Glacier National ParkOn.\n\n* WHEN...Until noon MDT today.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\nCreeks and streams may rise out of their banks. Flooding may occur\nin poor drainage and urban areas.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Ongoing precipitation west of the Continental Divide this morning\nwill keep concerns for minor flooding.\n- https://www.weather.gov/mso/hydrology",
                "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be alert for possible Flood\nWarnings. Those living in areas prone to flooding should be prepared\nto take action should flooding develop.",
