                "senderName": "NWS Honolulu HI",
                "headline": "Flood Watch issued September 8 at 3:28AM HST until September 8 at 6:00PM HST by NWS Honolulu HI",
                "description": "Trailing moisture along the eastern flank of Hurricane Lowell will\nbring periods of heavy rain to the main Hawaiian Islands through this\nafternoon.\n\n* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...Oahu, Maui County, Big Island.\n\n* WHEN...Through this afternoon.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flood prone roads and other low lying areas may be closed\ndue to elevated runoff and overflowing streams. Urban areas may\nreceive more significant flooding and property damage due to rapid\nrunoff.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Trailing moisture along the eastern flank of Hurricane Lowell\nwill bring periods of heavy rain to the main Hawaiian islands\nthrough this afternoon.",
                "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be prepared to take action\nshould Flash Flood Warnings be issued.",
