                "headline": "Flood Watch issued September 8 at 1:49AM MDT until September 8 at 6:00PM MDT by NWS Albuquerque NM",
                "description": "* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall is possible.\n\n* WHERE...A portion of central New Mexico, including the following\narea, South Central Mountains.\n\n* WHEN...From 11 AM MDT this morning through this afternoon.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations\ndownstream of the South Fork and Salt wildfire burn scars.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Monsoon moisture and atmospheric instability will be present this\nafternoon, leading to the development of strong, slow- moving\nthunderstorms over the Sacramento mountains. These slow-moving\nstorms will be capable of producing rainfall rates of 1 to 2\ninches per hour which may lead to excessive runoff on the\nvulnerable South Fork and Salt burn scars. These burn scars are\nvery susceptible to flash flooding.\n- http://www.weather.gov/abq/EmergencyPrepFlood",
                "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be prepared to take action\nshould Flash Flood Warnings be issued.",
